---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";
import Dashboard from "../components/Dashboard.astro";
import FileSystemVisualizer from "../components/FileSystemVisualizer.astro";
import Terminal from "../components/Terminal.astro";
import LessonPanel from "../components/LessonPanel.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Global Application Shell -->
  <div class="flex flex-col min-h-screen">
    <!-- SEO: indexable homepage text (server-rendered) -->
    <section class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-10">
      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
        BashQuest — interactive terminal sandbox for practice linux commands
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 body-md text-body">
        BashQuest is a browser-based bash learning platform designed for one
        goal: help you confidently practice linux commands and bash scripting
        without breaking your system.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold text-ink">
        Practice linux commands online, with instant feedback
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 body-sm text-body">
        Learning the command line is easier when you can try things immediately.
        BashQuest provides an interactive terminal sandbox where you can run
        real shell-style commands against a simulated Linux filesystem. Instead
        of watching videos or reading static examples, you build skill by
        completing short quests that guide you step-by-step—then you verify your
        output right inside the browser.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 body-sm text-body">
        Each quest focuses on a practical command-line skill: exploring
        directories, listing files, searching text, using pipes, understanding
        permissions, and writing small bash scripts. As you progress, the tasks
        become more realistic so your learning transfers to your real computer.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold text-ink">
        A virtual Linux terminal emulator with gamified bash tutorials
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 body-sm text-body">
        BashQuest acts like a linux terminal emulator, but with structured
        learning built in. The experience is gamified: you unlock quests in a
        curriculum tree, earn XP, and collect badges. That means every practice
        session has a clear purpose.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 body-sm text-body">
        The virtual environment is safe. You can experiment freely because your
        workspace is simulated. If you run a risky command or make a mistake, it
        stays within the interactive terminal sandbox and does not affect your
        machine. This makes it ideal for beginners and also useful for
        experienced users who want a fast way to refresh topics like
        redirection, wildcard matching, text processing, and permissions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold text-ink">
        Learn bash in browser: from one-liners to bash scripts
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 body-sm text-body">
        BashQuest is made for practice bash scripts online and for understanding
        how bash command-line tools work together. You will work through tasks
        that gradually expand your ability:
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside body-sm text-body space-y-1">
        <li>Explore and navigate the filesystem using familiar commands</li>
        <li>Read and manipulate files with text tools and patterns</li>
        <li>Use pipes and filters to transform output like a real workflow</li>
        <li>Practice wildcard matching and command substitution concepts</li>
        <li>Work with permissions and simulate safer command usage</li>
        <li>Write and test simple bash scripts in a guided environment</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="mt-4 body-sm text-body">
        When you finish a quest, you get confidence that your approach is
        correct, because the system checks your results. This is similar to an
        online bash compiler workflow—except your focus is learning and building
        intuition for everyday terminal work.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold text-ink">
        Why an online practice environment helps you improve faster
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 body-sm text-body">
        The fastest way to improve at the terminal is repetition with structure.
        BashQuest gives you both: short practice linux commands challenges and a
        curriculum that keeps you moving forward. You can focus on learning
        topics one at a time, while still working within a single consistent
        environment.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 body-sm text-body">
        Because the simulator is interactive, you can develop real muscle
        memory: typing commands, reading output, and iterating until you get the
        exact result. Over time, these steps become automatic, so you spend less
        effort on syntax and more effort on problem-solving.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 body-sm text-body">
        Whether you want to learn bash for school, build skills for Linux
        administration, or just become more comfortable with a linux terminal
        emulator, BashQuest is built to make practice feel productive and
        rewarding.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 body-sm text-body">
        Start practicing now by opening the interactive terminal sandbox from
        the dashboard. Choose a quest, run commands, and learn by doing.
        Bam—each completed step adds skill you can reuse in real-world terminal
        workflows.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Visible dashboard continues below -->

    <!-- Navbar -->
    <Navigation />

    <!-- Views Container -->
    <main class="flex-1 w-full relative">
      <!-- VIEW 1: Dashboard -->
      <section id="view-dashboard" class="block">
        <Dashboard />
      </section>

      <!-- VIEW 2: Interactive Sandbox Workspace -->
      <section
        id="view-sandbox"
        class="hidden lg:h-[calc(100vh-64px)] lg:overflow-hidden overflow-y-auto"
      >
        <div
          class="w-full py-4 lg:py-6 px-4 md:px-8 flex flex-col lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 h-auto lg:h-full min-h-0"
        >
          <!-- Left Column: Lesson Instructions Panel (5 cols) -->
          <div class="lg:col-span-5 h-auto lg:h-full min-h-0">
            <LessonPanel />
          </div>

          <!-- Right Column: Visual Explorer & Terminal (7 cols) -->
          <div
            class="lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col gap-6 h-auto lg:h-full min-h-0"
          >
            <!-- Filesystem Visual Explorer -->
            <div class="flex-1 min-h-[180px] lg:min-h-0">
              <FileSystemVisualizer />
            </div>

            <!-- Terminal Simulator Box -->
            <div class="flex-1 min-h-0">
              <Terminal />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- Reusable Bottom Footer Component -->
    <Footer />

    <!-- GNU Nano Text Editor Mockup Modal (Vercel-inspired dark overlay) -->
    <div
      id="modal-nano-editor"
      class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4 bg-black/75 backdrop-blur-xs hidden select-none"
    >
      <div
        class="w-full max-w-3xl h-[85vh] bg-[#121212] text-[#d4d4d4] font-mono text-[13px] rounded-lg border border-white/10 shadow-2xl flex flex-col overflow-hidden animate-in fade-in zoom-in-95 duration-200"
      >
        <!-- Nano Header -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-2 text-center text-white border-b border-white/5 relative flex justify-between select-none"
        >
          <span class="font-bold">GNU nano 7.2 equivalent</span>
          <span id="nano-filename" class="font-bold text-success"
            >File: server.conf</span
          >
          <span id="nano-modified" class="text-orange-400 font-semibold"></span>
        </div>

        <!-- Textarea Body -->
        <div
          class="flex-1 p-4 bg-[#121212] relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col"
        >
          <textarea
            id="nano-textarea"
            class="flex-1 w-full bg-transparent border-none outline-none resize-none font-mono text-[13px] text-white caret-white focus:ring-0 focus:outline-none p-0 m-0 leading-relaxed overflow-y-auto"
            placeholder="Type file contents here..."
            spellcheck="false"></textarea>
        </div>

        <!-- Shortcut Commands Guide (traditional Nano layout) -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#1a1a1a] p-3 border-t border-white/5 text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-mute grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-6 gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 select-none border-b border-white/5"
        >
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^G</span
            > Get Help
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^O</span
            > Write Out
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^W</span
            > Where Is
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^K</span
            > Cut Text
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^J</span
            > Justify
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^C</span
            > Cur Pos
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^X</span
            > Exit
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^R</span
            > Read File
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^\</span
            > Replace
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^U</span
            > Paste Text
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^T</span
            > To Spell
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="text-white font-bold bg-[#333] px-1 py-0.5 rounded-xs mr-1"
              >^_</span
            > Go To Line
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Save CTAs Bar -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-3 border-t border-white/10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-2 select-none"
        >
          <span class="text-[11px] text-[#888]"
            >Tip: Press Ctrl+O to Save, Ctrl+X to Save & Exit</span
          >
          <div class="flex gap-2">
            <button
              id="btn-nano-cancel"
              class="h-8 px-4 rounded-sm border border-white/10 text-white hover:bg-white/5 text-xs font-semibold cursor-pointer"
            >
              Cancel
            </button>
            <button
              id="btn-nano-save"
              class="h-8 px-4 rounded-sm bg-violet text-white hover:opacity-90 text-xs font-semibold cursor-pointer border-none"
            >
              Save Changes
            </button>
            <button
              id="btn-nano-exit"
              class="h-8 px-4 rounded-sm bg-[#ffffff] text-[#000000] hover:bg-[#eaeaea] text-xs font-semibold cursor-pointer border-none"
            >
              Save & Exit
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  declare global {
    interface Window {
      appState: any;
    }
  }

  import { FileSystem, ShellSession } from "../lib/linuxEngine";
  import { lessons } from "../lib/lessons";

  // Global Client-Side State Manager
  class AppStateManager {
    state: any;
    constructor() {
      this.state = {
        xp: 0,
        completedLessons: [],
        activeView: "dashboard",
        activeLessonId: 1,
        streak: 0,
        lastCompletedDate: null,
        fsTree: null,
        lessonStartTrees: {},
        installedPackages: [
          "pwd",
          "whoami",
          "clear",
          "help",
          "cd",
          "ls",
          "mkdir",
          "touch",
          "cat",
          "echo",
          "rm",
          "cp",
          "mv",
          "chmod",
          "grep",
          "wc",
          "uniq",
          "sort",
          "man",
          "apt",
          "df",
          "du",
          "free",
          "uptime",
          "uname",
          "ps",
          "top",
          "htop",
          "kill",
          "sleep",
          "jobs",
          "fg",
          "ping",
          "ip",
          "curl",
          "find",
          "history",
          "systemctl",
          "nano",
          "bash",
          "sed",
          "awk",
          "cut",
          "tr",
          "ln",
          "tar",
          "chown",
          "export",
          "env",
          "xargs",
          "head",
          "tail",
          "less",
          "more",
          "journalctl",
          "which",
          "alias",
          "crontab",
          "useradd",
          "passwd",
          "su",
          "ssh",
          "scp",
        ],
      };

      this.init();
    }

    init() {
      // 1. Load progress from localStorage if it exists
      this.loadFromStorage();

      // Check query parameter for view override (e.g. ?view=sandbox or ?view=dashboard)
      if (typeof window !== "undefined") {
        const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
        const viewParam = urlParams.get("view");
        if (viewParam === "dashboard" || viewParam === "sandbox") {
          this.state.activeView = viewParam;
        }
      }

      // 2. Setup initial filesystem instance
      this.resetFilesystem();

      // 3. Bind global event listeners
      this.bindEvents();

      // 4. Trigger initial rendering
      this.broadcastState();
      this.applyViewVisibility();
    }

    resetFilesystem() {
      // Create a fresh FS matching the active lesson's environment, or restore from existing tree
      const fs = new FileSystem(this.state.fsTree);

      // Perform customizations based on lesson needs
      // Ensure quest-required seeded files exist in the persisted filesystem
      const completed = this.state.completedLessons;

      // Quest 10/12: status.txt needed for Writing & Copying quests
      if (completed.includes(10) && !completed.includes(12)) {
        const statusNode = fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "status.txt");
        if (!statusNode) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "status.txt", "file", {
            content: "System Online\nAll Checks Green\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 13: Ensure log_1.txt, log_2.txt, log_3.txt exist for wildcard operations
      if (!completed.includes(13)) {
        const logFiles = [
          { name: "log_1.txt", content: "Log entry 1: System initiated.\n" },
          {
            name: "log_2.txt",
            content: "Log entry 2: System update started.\n",
          },
          {
            name: "log_3.txt",
            content: "Log entry 3: Database sync complete.\n",
          },
        ];
        for (const logFile of logFiles) {
          if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", logFile.name)) {
            fs.createNode("/home/learner", logFile.name, "file", {
              content: logFile.content,
            });
          }
        }
      }

      // Quest 14: Ensure downloads directory exists for removal quest
      if (!completed.includes(14)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "downloads")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "downloads", "dir");
        }
      }

      // Quest 16: Ensure names.txt exists for sort/uniq quest
      if (!completed.includes(16)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "names.txt")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "names.txt", "file", {
            content: "Alice\nBob\nAlice\nCharlie\nBob\nDavid\nCharlie\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 17: Ensure logs.txt exists for grep quest
      if (!completed.includes(17)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "logs.txt")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "logs.txt", "file", {
            content:
              "[INFO] Service started.\n[WARNING] High memory usage.\n[ERROR] Database connection failed.\n[INFO] User logged in.\n[ERROR] Failed to start database service.\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 18: Ensure deploy.sh exists for chmod quest (with default 644 permissions)
      if (!completed.includes(18)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "deploy.sh")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "deploy.sh", "file", {
            content:
              '#!/bin/bash\necho "Deploying application..."\necho "Done!"\n',
            permissions: "644",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 21: Ensure /etc/shadow exists for sudo quest
      if (!completed.includes(21)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/etc", "shadow")) {
          fs.createNode("/etc", "shadow", "file", {
            content:
              "root:$6$8zLx92xp$H9s2:18200:0:99999:7:::\nlearner:$6$1bYtM2op$P4w1:18200:0:99999:7:::\n",
            permissions: "000",
            owner: "root",
            group: "shadow",
          });
        }
      }

      // Seeds for new Quests
      // Quest 24/34: logs directory and logs files
      if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "logs")) {
        fs.createNode("/home/learner", "logs", "dir");
        fs.createNode("/home/learner/logs", "app.log", "file", {
          content:
            "Jul 3 12:00:00 [INFO] System boot up completed.\nJul 3 12:05:00 [INFO] Started web server service.\nJul 3 12:10:00 [WARNING] Disk space warning: 80% used.\n",
        });
        fs.createNode("/home/learner/logs", "security.log", "file", {
          content:
            "Jul 3 12:01:00 [INFO] User root logged in via ssh.\nJul 3 12:02:15 [WARNING] SSH Login failure from 192.168.1.100.\n",
        });
      }

      // Quest 38: server.conf
      if (!completed.includes(38)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "server.conf")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "server.conf", "file", {
            content: "host=127.0.0.1\nport=80\nmax_connections=100\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 45: reports.csv
      if (!completed.includes(45)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "reports.csv")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "reports.csv", "file", {
            content:
              "date,sales,visitors\njul 1,1200,450\njul 2,1500,500\njul 3,1800,600\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Quest 61: logs.tar.gz
      if (!completed.includes(61)) {
        if (!fs.getNodeByPath("/home/learner", "logs.tar.gz")) {
          fs.createNode("/home/learner", "logs.tar.gz", "file", {
            content: "tarball-archive-content\n",
          });
        }
      }

      // Keep state.fsTree in sync with the tree
      this.state.fsTree = fs.tree;

      // Cache starting tree for this quest if it hasn't been saved yet
      if (!this.state.lessonStartTrees) {
        this.state.lessonStartTrees = {};
      }
      const activeId = this.state.activeLessonId;
      if (!this.state.lessonStartTrees[activeId]) {
        this.state.lessonStartTrees[activeId] = JSON.parse(
          JSON.stringify(fs.tree),
        );
      }

      const session = new ShellSession(
        fs,
        "/home/learner",
        this.state.installedPackages,
      );

      window.appState = {
        ...window.appState,
        fs: fs,
        session: session,
        terminalCommands: [], // commands entered in this lesson session
        xp: this.state.xp,
        completedLessons: this.state.completedLessons,
        activeLessonId: this.state.activeLessonId,
        streak: this.state.streak,
        lastCompletedDate: this.state.lastCompletedDate,
      };
    }

    bindEvents() {
      // Listen for view changes from Navbar
      window.addEventListener("app:view-change", (e: any) => {
        this.state.activeView = e.detail.view;
        this.applyViewVisibility();
        this.saveToStorage();
        this.broadcastState();
      });

      // Listen for lesson selection
      window.addEventListener("app:select-lesson", (e: any) => {
        this.state.activeLessonId = e.detail.lessonId;

        // Reset filesystem sandbox to restore state or load current state
        this.resetFilesystem();

        this.saveToStorage();
        this.broadcastState();
      });

      // Listen for quest restore request
      window.addEventListener("app:restore-lesson", () => {
        const activeId = this.state.activeLessonId;

        // Restore filesystem tree of the current quest to its cached starting state
        if (
          this.state.lessonStartTrees &&
          this.state.lessonStartTrees[activeId]
        ) {
          this.state.fsTree = JSON.parse(
            JSON.stringify(this.state.lessonStartTrees[activeId]),
          );
        } else {
          this.state.fsTree = null;
        }

        // Reset completion status and deduct XP for this quest if it was completed
        if (this.state.completedLessons.includes(activeId)) {
          this.state.completedLessons = this.state.completedLessons.filter(
            (id: number) => id !== activeId,
          );
          const lesson = lessons.find((l) => l.id === activeId);
          if (lesson) {
            this.state.xp = Math.max(0, this.state.xp - lesson.xp);
          }
        }

        // Re-initialize a fresh filesystem using the restored tree
        this.resetFilesystem();

        this.saveToStorage();
        this.broadcastState();

        // Dispatch app:select-lesson to let the terminal and visual explorer know to reset
        window.dispatchEvent(
          new CustomEvent("app:select-lesson", {
            detail: { lessonId: activeId },
          }),
        );
      });

      // Listen for quest completions
      window.addEventListener("app:complete-lesson", (e: any) => {
        const { lessonId, xp } = e.detail;

        if (!this.state.completedLessons.includes(lessonId)) {
          this.state.completedLessons.push(lessonId);
          this.state.xp += xp;
        } else {
          // Practice Mode: 10% of lesson's normal XP, minimum of 5 XP
          const practiceXp = Math.max(5, Math.floor(xp * 0.1));
          this.state.xp += practiceXp;
        }

        // Always update streak on completion or practice mode
        this.updateStreak();

        this.saveToStorage();
        this.broadcastState();
      });

      // Listen for state reset request
      window.addEventListener("app:reset-state", () => {
        localStorage.removeItem("bashquest_state");
        this.state = {
          xp: 0,
          completedLessons: [],
          activeView: "dashboard",
          activeLessonId: 1,
          streak: 0,
          lastCompletedDate: null,
          fsTree: null,
          lessonStartTrees: {},
          installedPackages: [
            "pwd",
            "whoami",
            "clear",
            "help",
            "cd",
            "ls",
            "mkdir",
            "touch",
            "cat",
            "echo",
            "rm",
            "cp",
            "mv",
            "chmod",
            "grep",
            "wc",
            "uniq",
            "sort",
            "man",
            "apt",
            "df",
            "du",
            "free",
            "uptime",
            "uname",
            "ps",
            "top",
            "htop",
            "kill",
            "sleep",
            "jobs",
            "fg",
            "ping",
            "ip",
            "curl",
            "find",
            "history",
            "systemctl",
            "nano",
            "bash",
            "sed",
            "awk",
            "cut",
            "tr",
            "ln",
            "tar",
            "chown",
            "export",
            "env",
            "xargs",
            "head",
            "tail",
            "less",
            "more",
            "journalctl",
            "which",
            "alias",
            "crontab",
            "useradd",
            "passwd",
            "su",
            "ssh",
            "scp",
          ],
        };
        this.resetFilesystem();
        this.applyViewVisibility();

        // Return navbar tabs active state
        window.dispatchEvent(
          new CustomEvent("app:trigger-view-change", {
            detail: { view: "dashboard" },
          }),
        );

        this.saveToStorage();
        this.broadcastState();
      });

      // Listen for filesystem updates from the terminal
      window.addEventListener("app:filesystem-update", () => {
        if (window.appState && window.appState.fs) {
          this.state.fsTree = window.appState.fs.tree;
          this.saveToStorage();
        }
      });

      // Listen for package installation
      window.addEventListener("app:package-installed", (e: any) => {
        if (!this.state.installedPackages.includes(e.detail.package)) {
          this.state.installedPackages.push(e.detail.package);
          this.saveToStorage();
        }
      });

      // Listen for save export request
      window.addEventListener("app:export-save", () => {
        try {
          const saveCode = btoa(encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(this.state)));
          window.dispatchEvent(
            new CustomEvent("app:show-export-modal", { detail: { saveCode } }),
          );
        } catch (e) {
          console.error("Failed to export state", e);
        }
      });

      // Listen for save import request
      window.addEventListener("app:import-save", (e: any) => {
        const { saveCode } = e.detail;
        try {
          // Decode from base64 and parse JSON
          const decoded = decodeURIComponent(atob(saveCode));
          const parsedState = JSON.parse(decoded);

          // Basic validation to check that we have a valid state object
          if (
            !parsedState ||
            typeof parsedState !== "object" ||
            typeof parsedState.xp !== "number"
          ) {
            throw new Error("Malformed save code schema");
          }

          // Merge parsed state into current state
          this.state = {
            ...this.state,
            ...parsedState,
          };

          // Save to local storage
          this.saveToStorage();

          // Notify dashboard of success
          window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("app:import-success"));

          // Reload the page to fully reflect state changes
          window.location.reload();
        } catch (err) {
          console.error("Failed to import save code", err);
          window.dispatchEvent(
            new CustomEvent("app:import-error", {
              detail: {
                message:
                  "Invalid save code. Please ensure you copied the entire code correctly.",
              },
            }),
          );
        }
      });
    }

    updateStreak() {
      const today = new Date();
      today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0); // Normalize to midnight

      const lastDate = this.state.lastCompletedDate
        ? new Date(this.state.lastCompletedDate)
        : null;
      if (lastDate) lastDate.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

      if (!lastDate) {
        this.state.streak = 1;
      } else {
        const diffTime = today.getTime() - lastDate.getTime();
        const diffDays = Math.round(diffTime / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));

        if (diffDays === 1) {
          this.state.streak += 1;
        } else if (diffDays > 1) {
          this.state.streak = 1;
        }
      }
      this.state.lastCompletedDate = today.toDateString();
    }

    applyViewVisibility() {
      const viewDash = document.getElementById("view-dashboard");
      const viewSand = document.getElementById("view-sandbox");
      const footer = document.querySelector("footer");

      if (this.state.activeView === "dashboard") {
        viewSand?.classList.remove("animate-in", "fade-in", "duration-300");

        viewDash?.classList.remove("hidden");
        viewDash?.classList.add(
          "block",
          "animate-in",
          "fade-in",
          "duration-300",
        );
        viewSand?.classList.remove("block", "grid");
        viewSand?.classList.add("hidden");
        footer?.classList.remove("hidden");
      } else {
        viewDash?.classList.remove("animate-in", "fade-in", "duration-300");

        viewSand?.classList.remove("hidden");
        viewSand?.classList.add(
          "block",
          "animate-in",
          "fade-in",
          "duration-300",
        );
        viewDash?.classList.remove("block");
        viewDash?.classList.add("hidden");
        footer?.classList.add("hidden");

        // Autofocus terminal prompt when entering workspace
        setTimeout(() => {
          document.getElementById("terminal-input")?.focus();
        }, 100);
      }
    }

    broadcastState() {
      // Expose to globally accessible state objects
      if (window.appState) {
        window.appState.xp = this.state.xp;
        window.appState.completedLessons = this.state.completedLessons;
        window.appState.activeLessonId = this.state.activeLessonId;
        window.appState.streak = this.state.streak;
      }

      window.dispatchEvent(
        new CustomEvent("app:state-updated", {
          detail: this.state,
        }),
      );
    }

    saveToStorage() {
      localStorage.setItem("bashquest_state", JSON.stringify(this.state));
    }

    loadFromStorage() {
      const saved = localStorage.getItem("bashquest_state");
      if (saved) {
        try {
          const parsed = JSON.parse(saved);
          this.state = { ...this.state, ...parsed };
        } catch (e) {
          console.error("Failed to parse storage, using defaults", e);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Initialize State Manager on DOM load
  document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    new AppStateManager();

    // Nano Text Editor Overlay Management
    let currentNanoFile = "";
    let currentNanoPath = "";

    window.addEventListener("app:open-nano", (e: any) => {
      const { filename, currentPath, content } = e.detail;
      currentNanoFile = filename;
      currentNanoPath = currentPath;

      const modal = document.getElementById("modal-nano-editor");
      const textarea = document.getElementById(
        "nano-textarea",
      ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
      const title = document.getElementById("nano-filename");
      const modified = document.getElementById("nano-modified");

      if (title) title.textContent = `File: ${filename}`;
      if (modified) modified.textContent = "";
      if (textarea) textarea.value = content;

      modal?.classList.remove("hidden");
      setTimeout(() => textarea?.focus(), 100);
    });

    document.getElementById("nano-textarea")?.addEventListener("input", () => {
      const modified = document.getElementById("nano-modified");
      if (modified) modified.textContent = "[ Modified ]";
    });

    document
      .getElementById("nano-textarea")
      ?.addEventListener("keydown", (e: any) => {
        if (e.ctrlKey && e.key === "o") {
          e.preventDefault();
          saveNanoContent(false);
        } else if (e.ctrlKey && e.key === "x") {
          e.preventDefault();
          saveNanoContent(true);
        }
      });

    function saveNanoContent(shouldExit = false) {
      const textarea = document.getElementById(
        "nano-textarea",
      ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
      const content = textarea ? textarea.value : "";

      if (window.appState && window.appState.fs && currentNanoFile) {
        const fs = window.appState.fs;

        // Find existing or create new file
        const existing = fs.getNodeByPath(currentNanoPath, currentNanoFile);
        if (existing && existing.type === "file") {
          existing.content = content;
        } else {
          fs.createNode(currentNanoPath, currentNanoFile, "file", { content });
        }

        // Dispatch save event to update visual explorer
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("app:filesystem-update"));

        // Notify user in terminal
        window.dispatchEvent(
          new CustomEvent("app:print-terminal", {
            detail: {
              text: `[ File '${currentNanoFile}' saved successfully ]`,
            },
          }),
        );

        const modified = document.getElementById("nano-modified");
        if (modified) modified.textContent = "";
      }

      if (shouldExit) {
        document.getElementById("modal-nano-editor")?.classList.add("hidden");

        // Autofocus terminal input when exiting nano
        setTimeout(() => {
          document.getElementById("terminal-input")?.focus();
        }, 50);
      }
    }

    document
      .getElementById("btn-nano-cancel")
      ?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        document.getElementById("modal-nano-editor")?.classList.add("hidden");
        setTimeout(() => {
          document.getElementById("terminal-input")?.focus();
        }, 50);
      });
    document.getElementById("btn-nano-save")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      saveNanoContent(false);
    });
    document.getElementById("btn-nano-exit")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      saveNanoContent(true);
    });
  });
</script>
